{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966530,"nonce":"xbky7sp/qiiF8bQP9eH7I4uJp9M=","title":"Drive the DSL's FSMs through Zyntax fibers and effects","message":"An `fsm` declaration should lower to an `@effect` fiber whose handler\nowns its context, replacing the host-side registry that keyed a\nmachine's state by the FSM's name. A name gives one machine per\nprocess; a fiber has no name to collide over, so a mount constructs a\nmachine, holds the token, and two mounts of one component get separate\nstate and separate context.\n\nLive on `wip/fsm-machine-scope`, 71 commits ahead of main, 46 of them\nthis work. Tip `e3cecb14`. It is parked, not abandoned, and must not be\nsquashed into or dropped from main's history.\n\n**Standing.** Per-instance state and per-instance context both work.\nMachines execute every transition. Data guards fire on the event that\nsatisfies them. A component can declare the FSM it owns, a body that\nreads one opens its own scope, and the imported-FSM cases pass.\n\n**Why it is parked.** `main` carries a revert of an earlier attempt\n(\"machines execute transitions and own their context\") plus a follow-up\nthat gives an fsm a type and registers its event enum. Merging the\nbranch as it stands would silently reinstate what that revert removed,\nso the two lines have to be reconciled deliberately.\n\n**Known blocker.** `cn_playground_compiles` fails: `forms$FormWidgets$view`\ntakes no arguments but is called with one from `__blinc_with_3$view`.\n`inject_user_view_instance_id_params` walks one program's declarations,\nso a view reaching the entry module through an ES6 import never gets the\ninstance-id parameter its call site expects. This sits on the boundary\nbetween this work and multi-module compilation.\n\nDesign notes for this work live in memory under the FSM-as-fiber,\nsignals-are-effect-handles and program-driven-FSM-scope entries.","files":null}]}